  "summary": "Disconnects only the offending peer rather than all peers sharing an IP address during peer discouragement. In `MaybeDiscourageAndDisconnect`, it targets the individual node via `fDisconnect` instead of calling `DisconnectNode` with an address subnet.",
  "problem": "When a peer misbehaves, `MaybeDiscourageAndDisconnect` disconnects every connection sharing that peer's IP address. For inbound connections routed over Tor exit nodes, an attacker sending an invalid message can intentionally disconnect all other honest inbound peers using the same exit node.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description and commit d698b75f8b: \"If an attacker connects to the node through the same exit node and sends an invalid message, they can cause every inbound peer sharing the exit node's IP to get disconnected. Fix this by only disconnecting the misbehaving CNode rather than every CNode sharing the IP.\""
  ],
